## Installation

{{#if (eq packageKind 'config')}}
```sh
pnpm add -D @sgx4u/{{packageName}}          # pnpm
npm install --save-dev @sgx4u/{{packageName}}    # npm
yarn add --dev @sgx4u/{{packageName}}       # yarn
```
{{else}}
```sh
pnpm add @sgx4u/{{packageName}}       # pnpm
npm install @sgx4u/{{packageName}}    # npm
yarn add @sgx4u/{{packageName}}       # yarn
```
{{/if}}

Requires Node `>=22.12`. The package publishes ESM (`import`) and CommonJS (`require`). The export map lists `@sgx4u/source` before `import` and `require`, pointing at `src/index.ts`. TypeScript uses that condition when `customConditions` includes `@sgx4u/source`.

<p align="right">(<a href="#readme-top">back to top</a>)</p>

